WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.314
Welcome to OurWater.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:08.914
After this video you will know every part of your Home
page, in both the Easy view and the Advanced view,

00:00:09.034 --> 00:00:11.650
and you will know which view suits you.

00:00:12.483 --> 00:00:14.475
This is your Home page.

00:00:14.595 --> 00:00:20.451
It is the first page you see each time you open
OurWater, and it always starts with a welcome.

00:00:21.283 --> 00:00:23.587
Home comes in two views.

00:00:23.707 --> 00:00:27.979
Easy is the short, simple one, and it is what
you see now.

00:00:28.099 --> 00:00:31.123
Advanced adds a summary and more shortcuts.

00:00:31.243 --> 00:00:33.811
The switch is at the top of the menu.

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:37.929
This line says how many stations you look
after.

00:00:38.049 --> 00:00:43.905
A station is any water point you measure, such
as a well, a rain gauge or a check dam.

00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:47.117
Below are six big buttons.

00:00:47.237 --> 00:00:49.373
Each one opens a page.

00:00:49.493 --> 00:00:54.293
For everyday jobs you do not even need the
menu, because they are all here.

00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:58.213
Add a measurement is the button you will use
most.

00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:01.453
It opens the form where you record what you
saw.

00:01:01.573 --> 00:01:06.733
If you look after only one station, it opens
that station's form straight away.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.502
My stations is your list of water points.

00:01:10.622 --> 00:01:14.438
Open one to see its details, or add a new
station.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:18.466
My measurements shows everything you have
recorded.

00:01:18.586 --> 00:01:21.586
You can search it, and correct a mistake.

00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:26.233
My weather shows the forecast and the recent
rain for a place,

00:01:26.353 --> 00:01:29.473
so you can plan before you walk to the field.

00:01:30.283 --> 00:01:32.563
Messages is your mailbox.

00:01:32.683 --> 00:01:38.779
When something is waiting for you, a small red number
appears on its corner, like the 2 you see now.

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:41.587
With no mail, there is no number.

00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:48.561
If someone invites you to join a team or an organisation,
a card appears here, under the welcome,

00:01:48.681 --> 00:01:51.153
with Accept and Decline buttons.

00:01:51.273 --> 00:01:53.145
There is none today.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:59.662
Learn about water has short lessons on groundwater,
rain, and how to keep good records.

00:02:00.483 --> 00:02:03.939
Under the buttons is a map called Where your
stations are.

00:02:04.059 --> 00:02:06.819
It shows your own stations as pins.

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:10.755
Drag it to move, and use plus and minus to
zoom.

00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:15.015
If you lose your stations, click the target
button.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:18.975
The map moves so that every one of your
stations is in view.

00:02:19.783 --> 00:02:26.071
The Map button in the corner opens the big map, with
everyone's stations, a search box and filters.

00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:29.403
Now click Advanced in the switch.

00:02:29.523 --> 00:02:34.443
Home changes at once, and OurWater remembers
your choice for next time.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:39.714
Advanced Home starts with your monitoring
summary, in two cards.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:43.026
The first counts the monitoring stations you
can see.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:50.306
The second card is your last measurement: the value,
what was measured, how long ago, and where.

00:02:50.426 --> 00:02:53.738
If it was long ago, it may be time for a
visit.

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.502
Next comes the same map of your stations.

00:02:58.317 --> 00:03:01.917
Then a question: What measurement would you
like to add?

00:03:02.037 --> 00:03:07.293
Click the picture that matches your water source,
and the form opens for that kind of station.

00:03:08.117 --> 00:03:10.637
Only four are shown at first.

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:16.901
Show all station types opens the rest, from
rivers and springs to ponds and hand pumps.

00:03:17.717 --> 00:03:21.245
Click Show fewer, and the list folds back to
four.

00:03:21.365 --> 00:03:23.957
The button reads Show all again.

00:03:24.783 --> 00:03:30.735
Under the pictures are three shortcuts: Add a
station, Stations on map, and My weather.

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:38.510
Just below, an Organisation Admin also sees a
blue Admin summary card, marked Admin only,

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:44.630
with the organisation's totals: contributors,
stations, and measurements added.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:48.350
You are not an admin, so it does not appear
here.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.598
Last is Recent activity.

00:03:51.718 --> 00:03:57.958
It lists your newest measurements, with the kind of
water, the value, and how long ago you recorded it.

00:03:58.783 --> 00:04:04.735
View all on map opens the map on your own stations,
to see where those measurements were taken.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.614
So which view is for you?

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:13.590
Easy suits farmers, village volunteers, and
anyone who mostly records measurements.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:16.614
It has only what you need on a normal day.

00:04:17.417 --> 00:04:24.185
Advanced suits students, teachers, and coordinators,
who compare stations, watch the summary,

00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:26.681
and use the charts in the menu.

00:04:27.483 --> 00:04:29.883
You can switch at any time.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:32.571
Click Easy, and you are back.

00:04:32.691 --> 00:04:37.923
Nothing is lost, because both views show the
same stations and the same measurements.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.718
That is your Home page.

00:04:40.838 --> 00:04:45.302
Try the Advanced view for a day, and switch
back whenever you like.

00:04:45.422 --> 00:04:48.086
Thanks for helping look after our water.
